<ChapterLayout
  title="Load"
  number="01"
  problem="Preparation"
  definition="The load is the movement that prepares the body to move explosively, efficiently, and under control. The appearance may differ from player to player, but the purpose remains the same."
  purpose="Explosive movement does not happen efficiently from a standstill. The load starts movement—like revving the engine before the clutch drops."
  misconception="A load is not simply moving backward, and a bigger load does not automatically create more power. It should prepare movement, not add movement for its own sake."
